WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.030
OWARIMONOGATARI

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.490
SODACHI RIDDLE, PART TWO

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:03.870
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.240
FIVE YEARS AGO

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:06.620
<i>Five years ago.</i>

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:14.210
<i>In other words, what kind of a person
was Koyomi Araragi back in 7th grade?</i>

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:19.460
<i>Straightforward, pure, earnest...
what you could say about a normal child.</i>

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.130
<i>Young Araragi was mediocre,</i>

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:25.970
<i>but if you still tried to find something
special about him, it'd have to be</i>

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:31.060
<i>the fact that both his parents were police officers
whose purpose in life was justice, peace, and safety.</i>

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.110
<i>Under their influence,
the personality known as me had been created.</i>

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:40.650
<i>Young Araragi was, in that sense,
a boy who had a fairly strong sense of justice.</i>

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.780
<i>The story of five years ago.</i>

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:46.410
<i>This boy, right when first term was finishing,
was panicking just a little bit.</i>

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.660
<i>Not just a little.
He may have been panicking quite a bit.</i>

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:56.580
<i>Because the results of the recently returned
final exam weren't all that great.</i>

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:58.590
<i>Especially math.</i>

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.130
<i>He thought things would be bad
the way he was going.</i>

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.720
<i>He thought he wouldn't be able
to proceed righteously the way he was going.</i>

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:12.230
<i>More than math, he was embarrassed by the fact
that he couldn't fulfill the just cause of "learning."</i>

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.700
<i>Back then, I didn't know
about the "Monty Hall problem."</i>

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:53.240
<i>But I was interested in the problem
that was suddenly thrust at me.</i>

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.340
SO YOU DID COME FOR ME, ARARAGI.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.590
THE FACT THAT YOU'RE HERE...
YOU WERE ABLE TO SOLVE THE LETTER QUIZ?

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:14.060
Solve... No, it hasn't been solved.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.730
I did change my answer,
but I don't know why "C" is correct.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:21.480
I SEE.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.730
THEN, FIRST OFF, I'LL START
BY EXPLAINING THAT PROBLEM IN DETAIL.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:26.480
COME INSIDE, ARARAGI.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.240
LET'S STUDY.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:34.950
LET'S BECOME WISER TOGETHER.

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:37.830
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:45.710
According to the sender's story,
the letter was sent to a few others as well.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:52.590
But apparently I was the only one who received the letter
that came here, to this ruined house.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.470
The only one to shamelessly show up.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.720
Shamelessly? Yeah, I guess shamelessly.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.480
THOUGH YOU COULD PROBABLY SAY
FALTERINGLY AS WELL.

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:01.140
At the least,
if it wasn't for that summer,

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:06.270
I think I would've been bitter about math
and probably would've grown to hate it.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:09.360
Maybe I wouldn't have even been able
to enter Naoetsu High.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.820
In any case, let's hear the continuation of the story.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:15.490
Of one summer <i>aventure</i> for Araragi-senpai.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:19.870
The continuation of the secret rendezvous
between this mysterious girl and Araragi-senpai.

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:21.210
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:25.590
And so, you call this the "Monty Hall problem."

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:28.590
This is interesting!
Are there more problems like this?

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:29.960
There are lots of them.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:35.140
I'll teach you as many as you want, Araragi,
if you come to like math a lot more.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:37.470
If you'll continue to love math.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.850
I'll love it!
I'll make sure to keep loving math!

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:42.850
Then...

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:46.230
Let's keep studying here, starting tomorrow.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:47.980
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:51.740
And so, from the end of the first term,
until the end of summer break,

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:55.070
I regularly came to this ruined house.

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:57.120
I kept studying together
with the mysterious girl.

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:00.750
"The most beautiful equation in human history."

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:04.120
She was the one who
taught me about Euler's Identity.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:10.380
Even now, I can recite from memory what you'd call
the "mathematics" that are useless, even at school.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:15.340
So, for me, it didn't feel like
I was studying,

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:19.510
but more like I came to this ruined house
every day to play.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:24.520
If anything, this was like a secret base
for me and that girl.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.770
No, more like a secret cram school.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:28.650
A cram school, huh?

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:34.400
That girl was very particular about this location.
She said it was the only place she would study.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:39.780
The next day, when we met in the room
in the ruined house, she made a declaration.

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:43.200
There were conditions for us
to continue this study session.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:44.910
There were three conditions.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.040
One of them was that this would be
the location of the study session,

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:51.300
the farthest room on the second floor
of this ruined house.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:56.090
The second condition was that
our having study sessions like that

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:59.680
was to be a secret between the two of us.
Not to tell anyone about it.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:02.060
And the third condition was—

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:05.850
"Don't ask me what my name is."

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:08.480
"Don't probe into figuring out who I am."

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:12.610
"Don't ask me anything
if it's not about mathematics."

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:14.320
That was it.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:17.240
Was she a fairy of mathematics or something?

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.500
But, on the other hand...

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:29.040
She didn't ask for anything other than that.
Really, nothing else.

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.340
The three conditions,
and the first request she made was it.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:36.170
The fact she was teaching me without
getting anything in return started to bother me.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:39.430
So one day, I took some sweets with me, but...

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:42.680
I'm not doing this
because I want something in return.

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:45.770
I'm happy that I could
teach you mathematics.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:49.650
So please.
Please continue to love mathematics forever.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:51.650
...she said.

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:55.070
She sounds more and more
like a fairy of mathematics.

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:58.660
In any case, I went along
with all of her conditions,

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:01.280
and from then on,
I came to this ruined house every day.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:04.290
Really, every day, without skipping once?

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:05.790
But...

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:09.670
The study sessions abruptly ended one day.

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.670
It was on the last day of summer break.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:12.670
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:15.260
<i>The girl who was always there before me,</i>

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.760
<i>and had always prepared
the study sessions ahead of time,</i>

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:20.430
<i>was not there that one day.</i>

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:25.560
<i>Only that day... On that day,
for the first time...</i>

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.230
<i>No matter how much time passed,
no matter how long I waited,</i>

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:29.690
<i>she never showed up.</i>

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:33.860
AN ENVELOPE?

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:42.320
<i>Somehow, the 7th grader
Koyomi Araragi thought.</i>

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.330
<i>I will no longer...</i>

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:51.080
<i>...learn mathematics from her
in this place ever again.</i>

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:57.960
<i>In order to figure out her identity,
I started investigating in other classes.</i>

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.140
<i>Not only in my grade,
but among the upperclassmen...</i>

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:05.100
<i>There was no sight of the girl
I'd been seeing the entire summer.</i>

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:09.270
<i>As if her entire existence
had been wiped out,</i>

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:12.690
<i>young Araragi was...
right, trembling in fear.</i>

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.150
<i>So scary.</i>

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:17.730
<i>For the very first time,
at that moment I thought she was scary.</i>

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:20.990
<i>That's why I started
to avoid the ruined house...</i>

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:24.240
<i>And that's why I forgot about the girl.</i>

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:29.200
<i>But... The mathematics taught by the girl
in the ruined house was never forgotten.</i>

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:35.250
<i>As of the second term, young Araragi's grades
started to climb back up, mainly in mathematics.</i>

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:39.590
<i>In a way, his life perhaps
went back to the condition he was in</i>

00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:42.880
<i>before he started going regularly
to the ruined house.</i>

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:46.390
<i>Looking at the long-term effects,
perhaps nothing had changed.</i>

00:08:46.390 --> 00:08:49.810
<i>But there was one thing that
I could feel had changed for sure.</i>

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:54.980
<i>Young Araragi generally took a position
that sought justice from then on,</i>

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:59.570
<i>and because of that, he went out of control
every so often, only to deal with the repercussions.</i>

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:04.660
<i>But if you were talking purely about mathematics,
he was seeking amusement.</i>

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.780
<i>If he didn't have that,</i>

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:10.290
<i>I'm sure that back at that class assembly,
after his sense of righteous was shattered...</i>

00:09:10.620 --> 00:09:13.920
<i>...his heart would've had nothing left at all.</i>

00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:16.880
<i>That girl taught him
how amusing mathematics was.</i>

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:18.550
<i>How amusing life was.</i>

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.800
<i>How amusing the world was.</i>

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:23.930
<i>That's why I am who I am now.</i>

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.970
<i>I was created back in that summer.</i>

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:28.430
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:33.440
So to sum up,
that mysterious girl is Oikura-senpai, right?

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:37.610
No, wait, Araragi-senpai.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.440
This isn't what you'd call
an answer to a riddle.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:43.950
I'd actually say if, after all of this,
that girl wasn't Oikura,

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.780
your misdirection
was way too strong.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:48.620
It's what you'd call unfair.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:53.160
Then, Ougi, how do you explain that
after summer break, that girl, young Oikura,

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:56.420
was no longer at 701 Middle School?

00:09:56.420 --> 00:10:00.590
She just transferred schools.
But there's one hole left in this hypothesis.

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:07.390
In other words, this means Oikura-senpai
would've been your classmate at some point.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:09.800
Araragi-senpai, based on
what you've said up to now...

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:15.440
It seemed like you first met Oikura-senpai
after entering Naoetsu High School?

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:19.860
I thought that was when
I first met her.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:24.280
In other words, I had completely forgotten
about young Oikura.

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:27.990
I'd forgotten who was responsible
for me becoming so good at math.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:33.700
I'd forgotten how much I owed her,
and I treated her as a classmate.

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:37.920
She said that everything I had now
was all thanks to mathematics.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:40.750
Even the fact that I'm dating Senjyogahara.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:44.590
But did she really mean to say,
"It was all thanks to me"?

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:46.720
"I do like people who are happy," but...

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:51.100
"What I despise are people who don't know
the reason for their happiness," was it?

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:52.560
DESPISE

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.930
And what was it?

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:58.690
"I despise people who don't know
what they're made up of"?

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:04.190
When you bring back the forgotten memories,
those words really have a hidden meaning.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:08.280
In any case,
I need to apologize to Oikura tomorrow.

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:11.740
Though there's no way she'll start liking me,
since I'm someone she despises.

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:15.000
Nor will it do anything
to put her at ease.

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.870
But I need to apologize, so I will.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:20.580
Oh, you don't seem that enthusiastic.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.210
Of course not.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:25.920
It's not like I don't have complaints
about her as well, you know?

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:28.840
Like transferring schools.
Well, even if there were reasons behind it...

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.640
At the least, she could've
said something before she left.

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:35.220
Giving me nothing but an empty envelope?
I really don't get it.

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:36.930
SODACHI OIKURA

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:42.400
Besides, when we were reunited in class 1-3,
if she'd told me then,

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:44.440
I should've been able
to remember right there.

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:45.780
Even if you tell me now...

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:48.530
If she had told you then?

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:51.700
"That girl from back then was me, Araragi.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:55.290
It's been so long!
What, you've forgotten about me?

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:58.000
My gosh, that's the worst!
Geez, you really are cold!

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:01.790
But that's what's so won-der-ful about you!"

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:04.170
Or is something like that
what you wish she said?

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:09.670
I've never seen such a magnificent character
exist in this world, but, well...

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:14.550
You must be wondering
why she didn't tell you.

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:21.940
And you must also be wondering
why she left without saying anything.

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:26.730
If you don't think about it, even if
you apologize tomorrow, things may get worse.

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:31.200
A superficial apology will irritate the victim
more than anything else, you know.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:32.320
The victim?

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:37.240
Hey now, hold on a second, Ougi.
Isn't that saying a bit too much?

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:41.080
Indeed. Of course, it's not that
you're at fault, Araragi-senpai.

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:47.710
However, you are a fool, Araragi-senpai.
You're helpless. Helplessly so.

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:54.260
Ougi... What in the world
are you saying that you know?

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:56.260
I don't know anything.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:13:00.180
It's what you know, Araragi-senpai.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.390
Me?

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:07.940
Let's see. Just like when Oikura-senpai
was a young girl, I'll quiz you, then?

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:09.690
Question:

00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:14.360
Sodachi Oikura despises Koyomi Araragi
as if he killed her parents.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:18.830
That's because Koyomi Araragi
hadn't lived up to Sodachi Oikura's expectations.

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:22.870
That's why she transferred to a different school
without telling him anything.

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:27.090
Now, what did Sodachi Oikura hope for
from Koyomi Araragi?

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:29.800
What did she... hope for?

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:34.470
Hint: it has something to do
with the occupation of Araragi-senpai's parents.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:41.470
Thinking time: 120 seconds.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.480
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:53.990
ANSWER

00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:55.950
In other words, Oikura-senpai,

00:13:55.950 --> 00:14:01.750
by teaching Araragi-senpai the,
how to put it, "amusement in mathematics,"

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:03.870
she was seeking something
in compensation.

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:05.120
COMPENSATION

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:10.630
Speaking from a third-party perspective,
that first envelope is very suspicious.

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:12.880
It reeks of a trap.

00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:13.210
TRAP

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:14.130
A trap.

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:15.880
A fishhook, perhaps?

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:23.890
Her explanation that she sent letters to other students,
but you being the only one that showed up was a lie.

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:25.730
It was a complete fabrication.

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:28.650
In reality, she was aiming
to only hook you, Araragi-senpai.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:34.400
After finding out your math grades were poor,
Oikura-senpai decided to take advantage of that

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:38.410
and placed letters inside your shoe locker
whose contents would grab your attention.

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:42.950
A mathematical problem delivered to a boy
thinking he had to do something about his math grade...

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:45.040
Well, that's as good a lure as any.

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:49.130
That means I really did
shamelessly show up at her place...

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.290
Hey, Araragi-senpai.

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:59.390
You're familiar with the cram school ruins
my uncle Meme Oshino lived while in town, right?

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:04.810
Yeah. Well, like I said,
I've even slept there myself.

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:11.060
You also said this: that those ruins and these ruins
are rundown by about the same amount. Correct?

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:12.690
I did, so?

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:14.650
Isn't that a bit strange?

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:17.570
Why would a cram school that
went out of business a few years ago

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:21.620
and a house that was already in ruins five years ago,
be rundown to the same extent?

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.620
That's right, Araragi-senpai.

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:32.590
Five years ago... This place was not a ruined house.

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:36.460
The "ruined house"
was a misunderstanding on your part...

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:39.880
This used to be the house
Sodachi Oikura lived in.

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:41.220
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:45.970
Oikura's... residence?

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:50.350
Why was she always here
before you, Araragi-senpai?

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:55.860
Isn't it strange for someone to arrive first
to a meeting point every single time without fail?

00:15:57.320 --> 00:16:02.870
You should look at it that because this was her home,
Oikura-senpai was always able to wait for you.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:03.870
But...

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:06.750
Now, Araragi-senpai.

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:10.670
I know you're shocked by this,
and I'm sorry I have to whip you even further.

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:13.460
But this is the key point of my sleuthing.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:18.380
Why did Araragi-senpai think that five years ago,
the Oikura residence was a ruined house?

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:20.630
That's an error in my memory, isn't it?

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:24.640
No, just a misunderstanding.
Your memory itself is probably correct.

00:16:25.220 --> 00:16:28.350
Back then, the window in this room
was probably already broken like this.

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:31.140
You specifically stated as such already.

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:34.400
That's why this isn't an error in your memory,
but merely a misunderstanding.

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:39.650
Is it what you call domestic violence?

00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:41.150
Indeed.

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:47.290
It seems Oikura had to grow up
in quite the tragic family environment,

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:50.910
while you grew up all warm and fuzzy
in a peaceful family.

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:55.090
Even if you shoved the summer you came here
into a corner of your memory...

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:57.460
Even if you had packed it away
at the bottom of your memory...

00:16:57.460 --> 00:17:00.300
It perhaps isn't something
that you can be blamed for.

00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:07.060
The reason for her transfer in the second term,
in that case, is somewhat imaginable, too.

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:11.060
The family that was falling apart
probably fell apart completely.

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:15.400
Perhaps at that point,
Oikura's last name had changed?

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:19.480
And that was why when you were reunited with her
in class 1-3 of Naoetsu High,

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:22.820
you thought you'd never
met her before, Araragi-senpai.

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:25.660
Well, the thing is,
you should've recognized her face.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:28.160
In any case...

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:32.160
There's no doubt that the Oikura household
was at a critical point back then.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:35.670
And she wanted to do something about it.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.090
Something?

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:41.300
Something is literally something.
That's why she called you over, Araragi-senpai.

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:47.550
What Oikura-senpai had sought from
you as compensation was just that.

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:50.390
No, hold on a sec.
A family breakdown...

00:17:50.390 --> 00:17:54.770
Resolving a violent family breakdown...
That's too much to handle.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:57.940
What in the world was she expecting
from someone in 7th grade?

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:00.150
That's why I said, your parents.

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:01.150
Parents...

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:02.570
They're police officers, right?

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:06.570
The parents who showed the ways
of righteous to Araragi-senpai.

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:11.410
You were expected to report to those parents
the goings-on of the Oikura household.

00:18:13.910 --> 00:18:18.420
Even if so, I was forbidden from saying anything...
By Oikura herself.

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:21.670
To not tell anyone
I'm seeing Oikura here.

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:26.890
In the end, Oikura-senpai probably didn't want
to prosecute her own family.

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:31.430
Whether it was feeling guilt as a daughter
to rebuke her own parents,

00:18:31.930 --> 00:18:36.770
Or whether she feared retribution...
Perhaps it was both?

00:18:37.020 --> 00:18:42.400
In the end, she sought me to volunteer the condition
of the Oikura household to my parents.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:44.030
That's what she had intended.

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:47.910
I didn't do anything
that Oikura had hoped for.

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:54.080
But I absorbed all of the knowledge
that Oikura had given me to my heart's content.

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:59.080
<i>The empty envelope Oikura
had taped underneath the tea table</i>

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:01.880
<i>was an accurate depiction
of who I was as a man.</i>

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:03.630
<i>Empty and disappointing.</i>

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:06.170
<i>I was a guy she couldn't count on.</i>

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:10.550
Well, that's the gist of it.

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:13.720
Araragi-senpai, if my memory
serves me correctly,

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:19.980
you started this investigation
to figure out why you were hated

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:22.820
by Oikura-senpai
as if you killed her parents.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:27.070
That objective, at this point in time,
has basically been completed.

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:31.570
Therefore, I believe it's about time
to start thinking about retreating from here.

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:35.950
If there's something you'd like to say in closing,
go ahead. Your final words.

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:40.330
I really am blessed right now.

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:43.040
It's true that everything is great,
and I'm happy.

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:46.090
I have friends, I have a lover,
and I have underclassmen.

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:49.130
I'm very, very happy.

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:50.930
But...

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:55.850
As happy as I am,
I've come to despise myself a little bit.

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:59.310
Then, that little bit
is how much I will love you.

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:01.650
Besides, Araragi-senpai.

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:05.980
Another way to look at this is that it's a good thing
you haven't grown to despise mathematics.

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:08.490
No doubt.

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:10.740
<i>It's true.</i>

00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:13.990
<i>No matter what I grow to despise,
even if I lose sight of righteousness...</i>

00:20:13.990 --> 00:20:15.870
<i>I will continue to love mathematics.</i>

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:21.370
<i>It's already become a curse of sorts.</i>

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:23.630
OWARIMONOGATARI
SODACHI RIDDLE

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:27.630
Ougi Oshino... Oshino's niece?

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:32.720
Oh, yeah. Thanks to her,
I figured out all sorts of things.

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:36.510
As expected of Oshino's relative,
it was pretty impressive sleuthing.

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:41.640
Without her, I wouldn't have been able to figure out
those mysteries yesterday or the day before.

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:50.650
Araragi, It pains me to add to things,
considering how you are now...

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:54.780
Araragi, it's not strange to figure out
that you hit a wall concerning math

00:20:54.780 --> 00:21:00.080
during the finals for your first term
in your 7th grade year.

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:04.920
And I think it's also possible to take advantage of that
by placing the "Monty Hall problem" in your shoe locker.

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:11.510
But... The key point about that plan,
the fact that your parents are police officers...

00:21:11.510 --> 00:21:14.050
How did Oikura find out about that?

00:21:15.010 --> 00:21:19.310
Wasn't that something
you did everything you could to hide?

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:25.610
<i>That's right. When it comes to that,
I have a habit of not answering even when asked,</i>

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.570
<i>to avoid extra, or unnecessary, troubles.</i>

00:21:30.610 --> 00:21:35.120
<i>But why... Why did Oikura know about that? How?</i>

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:40.790
Of course, there's the chance she just happened to know
because something caused her to find out.

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:45.710
Perhaps there's something else
between you and Oikura.

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:50.840
Some other memory you need to retrace,
another door you still need to open.

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:53.970
<i>A memory I need to retrace...</i>

00:21:58.350 --> 00:21:59.970
<i>Another door I still need to open...</i>

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:02.560
<i>Is there something else that I've forgotten,
on top of everything else?</i>

00:22:02.560 --> 00:22:05.770
FOOLISH

00:22:05.770 --> 00:22:09.690
<i>If so, just how foolish
is Koyomi Araragi?</i>

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:12.360
<i>Is there no end to my foolishness?</i>

00:22:13.530 --> 00:22:17.990
<i>"You're someone that I'd never forget about,"
was what Oikura said.</i>

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:22.120
<i>If that's the case, she's sure to remember.</i>

00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:27.670
<i>The fool from two years ago, from five years ago,
and from even before that.</i>

00:22:29.170 --> 00:22:31.840
<i>I've arrived in front of my classroom.</i>

00:22:32.630 --> 00:22:36.220
<i>Beyond this door, whether or not
Sodachi Oikura will be there is...</i>

00:22:36.510 --> 00:22:37.550
<i>...alas, a completely impossible proof.</i>

00:22:37.550 --> 00:24:20.187
ALAS, A COMPLETELY IMPOSSIBLE PROOF.
